^SAMPLE = GSM8322368
!Sample_title = SC_2D, scRNAseq [SC_2D-1]
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8322368
!Sample_status = Public on Apr 14 2026
!Sample_submission_date = Jun 11 2024
!Sample_last_update_date = Apr 14 2026
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = H9
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: H9
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: 2D culture
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The organoids were dissociated into single cells using the STEMdiff Cardiomyocyte Dissociation Kit (Stemcell Technologies, #05025). The cell suspension was then loaded into Chromium microfluidic chips for single-cell RNA sequencing.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The cell suspension was processed with 3’ (v2 or v3, depending on the project) chemistry and barcoded using a 10× Chromium Controller (10X Genomics). RNA from the barcoded cells was reverse-transcribed, and sequencing libraries were constructed using the Chromium Single Cell 3’ v2 (v2 or v3, depending on the project) reagent kit (10X Genomics), following the manufacturer’s instructions.
!Sample_data_processing = The demultiplexing, barcoded processing,gene counting and aggregation were made using the Cell Ranger software v7.0.0(https://support.10xgenomics.com/single-cell-gene-expression/software/pipelines/latest/what-is-cell-ranger)
